Hey! I'm an indie dev named Priya building a little physics sandbox game with my friend Owen. We want to create a repository called game-physics-sandbox. Since we're both contributing, we're thinking a main branch for stable code and dedicated development branches: dev-priya and dev-owen. Could you initialize the README.md file on main with: "# Game Physics Sandbox

A 2D sandbox for experimenting with rigid body dynamics and collision detection."? I'd also like a basic world.py file on main with: "# Physics world skeleton
class World:
    def __init__(self, gravity=-9.8):
        self.gravity = gravity
        self.bodies = []

    def step(self, dt):
        for body in self.bodies:
            body.velocity_y += self.gravity * dt"

I've been studying narrow-phase collision detection, so could you copy narrowphase.cpp from erincatto's box2d repository onto my branch? Owen has been focused on broad-phase detection, so could you also copy broadphase.cpp from bulletphysics' bullet3 repository onto his branch? Finally, please create a pull request from dev-priya to main with the title "Add physics world skeleton" and description "This PR adds the initial physics world skeleton that the collision systems will build on."
